---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Arrow from '../components/Arrow.astro';
import HeroDiagram from '../components/HeroDiagram.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';
import CommercialPillars from '../components/CommercialPillars.astro';
import ResearchCallout from '../components/ResearchCallout.astro';
---
<Layout title="File-level protection for a compromised world">
<section class="hero container"><div class="hero-copy"><span class="eyebrow"><span class="small-cross">+</span> BEYOND THE PERIMETER. INTO THE FILE.</span><h1>Protection that<br/>stays with<br/>the <span class="serif-word">file.</span><span class="lime-period">■</span></h1><p class="hero-positioning">Zero-trust data protection.<br/>Quantum-secure architecture.<br/>Software deployment without the rip-and-replace.</p><p class="hero-lead">Protect information at the data layer. Cyber Reliant separates and fragments protected data and cryptographic material, controlling access through an authorized reconstruction path.</p><div class="button-row"><a href="/request-demo" class="button button-dark">Request a demo <Arrow/></a><a href="/how-it-works" class="text-link">See how it works <span class="circle-arrow"><svg class="diagonal-arrow" width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 18 18 6M6 6h12v12" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"/></svg></span></a></div><div class="hero-footnote"><span class="mini-line"></span><span>Storage access is not file access.</span></div></div><div class="hero-visual"><HeroDiagram/></div></section>
<CommercialPillars/>
<section class="soft-section" id="evidence"><div class="section container">
  <div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">WHY BELIEVE IT</span><h2>Operational history.<br/>Independent research.</h2></div></div>
  <ResearchCallout/>
  <div class="company-proof"><div class="proof-heading"><h3>Credentials &amp; operational history</h3></div>
  <div class="proof-grid">
    <article><h4>11+ YEARS</h4><p>CSfC history</p></article>
    <article><h4>SINCE 2018</h4><p>Combat deployed</p></article>
    <article><h4>ZERO KNOWN BREACHES</h4><p>Of protected Top Secret data</p></article>
    <article><h4>PATENT-PENDING</h4><p>Software-based TRNG technology</p></article>
    <article><h4>SECURITY / INSURANCE SUPPORT</h4><p>Lloyd’s of London relationship</p></article>
  </div></div>
</div></section>
<section class="section container risk-section"><div><span class="eyebrow">ZERO TRUST, EXTENDED TO THE DATA ITSELF</span><h2>Storage access<br/>is not file access.</h2></div><div class="risk-copy"><p class="large-copy">Possessing the fragments is not the same as possessing the file.</p><p>Network or storage access does not automatically provide permission to read protected information. Application policy participates in the access decision; the authorized Cyber Reliant path brings the required fragments and cryptographic material together for reconstruction.</p><a class="text-link" href="/enterprise">A different starting point for enterprise security <Arrow/></a></div></section>
<section class="dark-section" id="quantum"><div class="section container split-content"><div><span class="eyebrow">QUANTUM SECURITY</span><h2>Protect against<br/>harvest now, decrypt later.</h2></div><div><p class="large-copy">More computing power does not supply missing protected components.</p><p>Conventional encryption generally relies on mathematical problems remaining computationally difficult. The AIA approach described in FDD’s research adds a requirement: obtain sufficient protected data fragments and cryptographic components before reconstruction or decryption is possible.</p><p>An information-theoretic approach is designed to address what an attacker possesses, as well as what an attacker can compute.</p><a class="text-link light-link" href="/technology#quantum">Explore the quantum-security research <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></div></section>
<section class="mechanism-section"><div class="container section"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">FOUR PARTS. ONE CONTROLLED ACCESS PATH.</span><h2>Protect the pieces.<br/>Control the whole.</h2></div><p>The architecture separates what is stored from what is required to make it readable.</p></div><div class="mechanism-grid mechanism-four"><a href="/how-it-works#fragment" class="mechanism-card"><span class="card-number">01 / FRAGMENT</span><div class="mini-art art-fragments"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></div><h3>Break the file<br/>into fragments.</h3><p>Divide the sensitive file into pieces for protection.</p><span class="card-link">Fragment <Arrow/></span></a><a href="/how-it-works#encrypt" class="mechanism-card"><span class="card-number">02 / ENCRYPT</span><div class="mini-art art-encrypt"><span>×</span><span>7</span><span>◇</span><span>+</span><b>⌑</b></div><h3>Encrypt<br/>the fragments.</h3><p>Protect the contents of the pieces before distributing them.</p><span class="card-link">Encrypt <Arrow/></span></a><a href="/how-it-works#separate" class="mechanism-card"><span class="card-number">03 / SEPARATE</span><div class="mini-art art-separate"><span>▥</span><i></i><span>◇</span></div><h3>Separate data<br/>from key material.</h3><p>Distribute protected file fragments while protecting cryptographic material through a separate path.</p><span class="card-link">Separate <Arrow/></span></a><a href="/how-it-works#reconstruct" class="mechanism-card"><span class="card-number">04 / RECONSTRUCT</span><div class="mini-art art-reconstruct"><span>▤</span><i></i><span>◇</span><b>↓</b></div><h3>Rebuild through<br/>authorized access.</h3><p>The controlled Cyber Reliant path brings the required pieces and cryptographic material together to produce readable data.</p><span class="card-link">Reconstruct <Arrow/></span></a></div></div></section>
<section class="section container app-section"><div class="application-visual"><div class="diagram-top"><span>APPLICATION ACCESS</span><span>FIG. 02</span></div><div class="app-path"><span class="app-symbol">▦</span><div><strong>Authorized application</strong><small>Permitted by application policy</small></div><span class="access-pill allowed">ALLOW</span></div><div class="app-path"><span class="app-symbol">▧</span><div><strong>Unapproved application</strong><small>Not permitted by application policy</small></div><span class="access-pill blocked">BLOCK</span></div><div class="access-gateway"><span>APPLICATION-LEVEL CONTROLS</span><span>↓</span></div><div class="protected-file"><span>▤</span><div><strong>Protected file access</strong><small>Controlled decryption + reconstruction</small></div><span class="status-dot"></span></div><p class="small-note">Conceptual policy flow. Enforcement depends on implementation and configuration.</p></div><div><span class="eyebrow">ACCESS IS MORE THAN A USERNAME</span><h2>The filter participates<br/>in rebuilding the file.</h2><p>Application policy determines which applications can proceed through the protected access path. Reconstruction then requires more than an ordinary file read.</p><p>The Cyber Reliant Windows filter participates in identifying the correct fragments, obtaining required cryptographic material, decrypting the fragments and reconstructing the file.</p><a class="text-link" href="/technology#windows">Explore the access architecture <Arrow/></a></div></section>
<section class="soft-section" id="deployment"><div class="section container"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">SOFTWARE DEPLOYMENT</span><h2>Security without<br/>the rip-and-replace.</h2></div><p>Add protection at the data layer rather than beginning with a wholesale replacement of networks, storage or endpoint hardware.</p></div><div class="use-case-grid"><article><span class="card-number">01 / PRESERVE</span><h3>Keep infrastructure investments.</h3><p>Design protection around the environments you already operate, rather than rebuilding them around a new security appliance.</p></article><article><span class="card-number">02 / DEPLOY</span><h3>Start with software.</h3><p>The core data-protection approach is software-based, avoiding specialized encryption hardware solely to implement that core architecture.</p></article><article><span class="card-number">03 / ADAPT</span><h3>Tailor the deployment.</h3><p>Evaluate distributed, hybrid, cloud, edge and constrained environments against the architecture and your operational requirements.</p></article></div><details class="technical-disclosure"><summary>Deployment fit and hardware boundaries</summary><p>The FDD pilot described a vendor/service-provider-agnostic, distributed, multiplatform approach that can be customized to the customer’s existing architecture. Deployment is tailored to application compatibility, connectivity and recovery needs. The upcoming network version uses an HSM-based key architecture.</p></details><a class="text-link" href="/request-demo?interest=Enterprise">Discuss fit with your existing environment <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></section>
<section class="network-banner"><div class="container network-inner"><span class="outline-tag">UPCOMING NETWORK VERSION</span><h2>The data path and the key path<br/>are separate by design.</h2><div><p>The upcoming network architecture fragments the cryptographic material itself and protects multiple key components through the HSM architecture. Both paths meet at authorized Cyber Reliant reconstruction.</p><a class="text-link light-link" href="/technology#network">Inside the network architecture <Arrow/></a></div></div></section>
<section class="section container"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">DIFFERENT MISSIONS. THE SAME STAKES.</span><h2>For data you can’t<br/>afford to expose.</h2></div></div><div class="audience-cards"><a class="audience-card" href="/enterprise"><div class="audience-card-top"><span class="tiny-label">01 / ENTERPRISE</span><Arrow/></div><h3>Protect the information<br/>your business depends on.</h3><p>Intellectual property. Financial records. Sensitive operational files. Start with the data that matters most.</p><span class="text-link">Explore enterprise</span></a><a class="audience-card government-card" href="/government"><div class="audience-card-top"><span class="tiny-label">02 / GOVERNMENT</span><Arrow/></div><h3>Put sensitive mission<br/>data at the center.</h3><p>Evaluate file-level protection against your mission requirements, deployment constraints and security policies.</p><span class="text-link">Explore government</span></a></div></section>
<CTA title="Bring the data. Bring the environment." text="Explore your Zero Trust boundaries, long-term quantum exposure and deployment fit in one focused technical briefing."/>
</Layout>
